body:
We discussed this in the most recent WHATNOT, and we seemed to reach somewhat of a conclusion: throwing is the least desired solution here as it poses some webcompat issues and doesn't seem well motivated otherwise. The other solutions boil down to essentially: return early on request close (the current chrome behaviour) or establish/destroy a closewatcher in sync with the open attribute regardless of disconnected state (the behaviour specced in @lukewarlow's PR).

We're unsettled on which of these to go with, but it sounds as though the group was perhaps steering toward early return.

@domenic do you have thoughts?
